USOS 3.1.2-usos11-diag patch 0013 (2026-10-17): one-shot BSP NMI snapshot for the Windows 2000 ACPI diagnosis (DIAGNOSTIC VARIANT ONLY)

Design and code by Codex (its "0012-one-shot-bsp-nmi-diagnostic" for the
X470 rounds of 2026-10-16/17, firmware-13 c1f1c4fa..., commit c6222cd of
codex/w2k-watcher-results), taken without its ACPI table filter parts
(src/usos_acpi10.*, usos_w2k_hpet_filter.inc: production patch 0012 does
that with our own code). Applies on 0001-0012 including the 0011 watcher.

Only in the diagnostic CSMWrap variant (tools/vendor/csmwrap/3.1.2-usos11-diag,
used by the Windows 2000 flow only when DATA ...\Unattended\w2k-diag.txt or
nmi-snapshot.txt exists) and only with csmwrap.ini acpi_legacy_fadt = true
and w2k_nmi_snapshot = true: the watcher helper core may send one NMI to the
boot CPU when the clock stops, and the NMI handler of the diagnostic usosvid
records its state into the watcher page. CONFIG_SDCARD is off in this
variant only, so SeaBIOS keeps its 6144-byte F-segment floor with the extra
helper code. Not part of the production series 3.1.2-usos11.

